BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Leatherqueer Picnic
DTSTART:20261024T140000
DTEND:20261024T140000
UID:88ac16681739b1483831440da7bc0aac@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Leatherqueer Picnic Saturday October 24th\, 2-5 pm. We
 ather Permitting! *If it’s raining\, we’ll reschedule for another time
 . This is a space for leatherqueers of marginalized genders to connect\, m
 ake friends\, and cruise. Flagging is encouraged! We will have optional na
 me tags and icebreaker prompts to help folks mingle comfortably. We’ll g
 ather in the southwest corner of the park\, near Banjara. Look for the Lea
 ther Pride flag to find us! This spot in the park is mixed sun and shade a
 nd has flat\, uneven grassy ground. If you like\, bring yourself a camp ch
 air\, picnic blanket\, pillow\, snacks\, whatever you’d like to have to 
 enjoy a nice afternoon in the park. Let’s be comfortable! A note on C0v1
 D: the limited data we have makes it difficult to assess the severity of t
 his ongoing pandemic. Let’s practice caring safety protocols and give ea
 ch other ample space. Bring a mask in case you want to get closer to skill
 -share or cruise etc. *If someone is wearing a mask\, wear one to approach
  them.* If you have any symptoms of illness or known/suspected recent expo
 sures\, please don’t come. Let’s make sure we have a healthy tomorrow 
 to meet again in the future. Christie Pits is at 750 Bloor St W in Toronto
 . It is accessible by car with street and lot parking nearby\, by subway v
 ia Line 2 at Christie station and by bus via route 126. There are two\, ge
 ndered\, wheelchair-accessible washrooms at the bottom of a steep hill wit
 h a paved path. Your organizers are @hollys_horny_home @pansybutch @beth_b
 ec0mes_her &amp\; @thekikikennedy. Inspired by similar gatherings across t
 urtle island\, with acknowledgement &amp\; appreciation to @mother.archety
 pe &amp\; @_wolfsmilk._ .\, @monster_femme\, @sharonpinkishere\, @chicagol
 eatherdykepicnic\, and many others. ‍
LOCATION:Christie Pits Park\, 750 Bloor Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/toronto-leatherqueer-picnic-6
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eternal Winter: VINTAGE SAPPHIC SALON
DTSTART:20261024T183000
DTEND:20261024T183000
UID:03d37c77a20f8e042543d6a03b46e7e5@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Step into Eternal Winter\, a cozy vintage sapphic salon where 
 stories\, style\, and poetry melt the frost away. Eternal Winter: VINTAGE 
 SAPPHIC SALON Date &amp\; Time: Saturday\, October 24\, 2026 | Doors Open 
 at 6:30 PM | Performance at 7:00 PM | Q&amp\;A at 8 PM | Mingling ‘till 
 9 PM Venue: The Green Room at Book Bar About this Event: Join émigré aut
 hor and scholar Veronika Sizova for an exclusive\, intimate evening of her
  sapphic prose + poetry performance within the curated\, vintage atmospher
 e of The Green Room. The evening will feature a live reading of passages f
 rom her sapphic romance novel «The Dawn of Eternal Winter» (Life Rattle 
 Press)\, exploring the intricate boundaries of lesbian desire in Saint Pet
 ersburg\, 1905. Guests will be treated to 2 complimentary signature cockta
 ils crafted specifically for this night alongside light hors d&#x27\;oeuvr
 es. Following the performance and a Q&amp\;A session\, a private signing a
 nd social mingling with other sapphics will take place. Dress-up is encour
 aged! Tickets Tier 1: General Admission — $25.00 CAD What is included: E
 ntry to the private reading session at The Green Room\, 2 drinks\, and lig
 ht gourmet appetizers. Tier 2: VIP Author’s Experience (Admission + Book
 ) — $40.00 CAD What is included: All benefits of Tier 1\, plus a guarant
 eed\, personally signed and dedicated copy of the debut novel «The Dawn o
 f Eternal Winter» Please note: This event is 21+\, wlw-only. Capacity is 
 limited to preserve the tight\, close-knit experience of the performance. 
 Early booking is highly recommended. ‍
LOCATION:600 Markham St\, 600 Markham St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/eternal-winter-vintage-sapphic-salon
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
