BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Connection Beyond Breath: Living Relationships with Our Dead
DTSTART:20261027T190000
DTEND:20261027T190000
UID:df67f60328935e3eb9a2454fd162122b@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. In this co
 llective conversation\, grievers are invited to connect over ways they are
  or want to be in relation with their dead. This is not an instructional s
 ession but rather a container for folks to share and hear about the variet
 y of ways our dead show up in our lives - in dreams\, memories\, conversat
 ions\, spaces\, through animal sightings\, cultural and spiritual practice
 s\, etc. - and how ongoing relationships with our dead can transform how w
 e live\, in tough\, tender\, and touching ways. Fueled by years of cultiva
 ting relationships with their dead\, Case hopes participants leave this co
 nversation both feeling more resourced to build and maintain relationships
  with theirs\, and imagining how we\, too\, will want to be remembered and
  connected with when we join them. “Time is queer and so is grief: grief
  queers time inexorably. Lose a friend and find how the lines between life
  and death are also a perpetual spectrum. Who knew loving our dead and nam
 ing our dying while trying to survive could be so fucking queer? I would l
 ove to meet you here.” ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/connection-beyond-breath-living-relationsh
 ips-with-our-dead
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
