BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Violet Hour Book Club Toronto Edition: De Profundis
DTSTART:20261102T190000
DTEND:20261102T190000
UID:c79fbad1850ca601f6d8276e9ff78db8@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the next meeting of the Toronto edition of the Vio
 let Hour Book Club (VHBC) at Another Story Bookshop! Join us for the sixth
  meeting of the Toronto edition of the Violet Hour Book Club (VHBC)\, a re
 ading and discussion group dedicated to exploring classic and contemporary
  2S/LGBTQ+ literature. Our next selection is Oscar Wilde&#x27\;s De Profun
 dis. A theatrical presentation of De Profundis (De Profundis: Oscar Wilde 
 in Jail\, adapted and directed by Gregory Prest) will also be presented at
  Soulpepper Theatre in Toronto from November 3–29. Violet Hour Book Club
  members are invited to attend the Tuesday\, November 3 performance as a g
 roup outing. Those who are interested are also welcome to meet for a drink
  at the theatre bar beforehand (as of 6 PM). Founded in Montreal in 2019\,
  VHBC has become an important gathering space for queer book lovers in the
  city\, fostering meaningful connections through a shared appreciation of 
 foundational classics and bold\, contemporary voices. The club provides an
  inclusive environment for lively\, thought-provoking conversations on boo
 ks\, literary culture\, and the craft of storytelling – cultivating dial
 ogue that is both intellectually stimulating and deeply personal. Everyone
  is welcome. Copies of the book will be available for guests at a 10% disc
 ount with the promo code VHBC. Please order online at anotherstory.ca. Abo
 ut the book A definitive new collection of Oscar Wilde’s best prison let
 ters and poetry\, with an introduction by Colm Toibin Bankrupt and with hi
 s reputation in ruins\, Oscar Wilde wrote the astonishing letter “De Pro
 fundis” to his lover\, Lord Alfred Douglas\, while in prison. Editor Col
 m Toibin\, the acclaimed author of The Blackwater Lightship\, The Master\,
  and Brooklyn\, describes it as Wilde’s “greatest piece of prose writi
 ng.” Also included is “The Ballad of Reading Gaol\,” Wilde’s most 
 famous poem and one of the greatest ballads in the English language\, as w
 ell as other letters Wilde wrote from prison that reveal the true effects 
 of incarceration on the people he met. Based on the Penguin Classics editi
 on of the Complete Letters\, this collection features a new introduction\,
  notes\, and appendices. ‍
LOCATION:Another Story Bookshop\, 315 Roncesvalles Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/violet-hour-book-club-toronto-edition-de-p
 rofundis
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Protecting Sobriety Through Loss
DTSTART:20261103T190000
DTEND:20261103T190000
UID:a5a05846b34391fd2d41ad0fc800cd91@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. In her lif
 e Jackie Clark has seen the overlapping power of queer and recovery commun
 ities. Getting sober after a devastating loss and staying sober through an
 other was one of the hardest things She&#x27\;s ever experienced\, and it 
 is only through deep connections with other people and a lot of truth tell
 ing that She managed. This session is for 2SLGBTQIA+ people in recovery (h
 owever they may define it)\, struggling with substance use\, or supporting
  friends and family through the same\, to connect about how death and grie
 f intersect with addiction and recovery. Participants can expect some fram
 ing\, a grounding meditation\, and some prompts for peer-sharing. Particip
 ate as much as you’re comfortable (just listening is okay too)! *A note 
 about language and perspective: I\, Jackie\, will facilitate with deep car
 e and a concerted effort to use language as inclusively as possible. I als
 o understand that everyone’s experiences with both addiction/substance u
 se disorders and with grief are extremely individual. I am not an expert\,
  but a peer with lived experience. * Please feel free to bring your own ex
 perience to the table\, and also leave behind any perspectives that do not
  resonate with or serve you. Jackie Clark (she/they) is a queer person fro
 m Battersea\, Ontario celebrating six years of sobriety. In her profession
 al life she works for a non-profit and on a farm –part of that work is a
 dvocating for and building community among queer and trans farmers. Outsid
 e of work she fills her days with fostering animals\, running in the woods
 \, and spending time with friends. After the loss of her best friend in 20
 19\, she worked towards harm reduction and then addiction recovery\, event
 ually spending a year facilitating meetings for folks recovering from all 
 types of substance use and behavioral addictions. She believes firmly in t
 he wisdom and power of queer community to hold each other safely as we nav
 igate grief. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/protecting-sobriety-through-loss
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exploring Gender and Sexuality Through Animal Role Play
DTSTART:20261103T200000
DTEND:20261103T200000
UID:32d7d0437047b59e1d8b159069570f1f@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Inside you there are two wolves.&quot\; Maybe they&#x27\;re bo
 th gay. US / International Attendees: This event is priced in CAD. At chec
 kout\, you will see the CAD price\, but your bank will automatically conve
 rt it to your local currency. See tickets for estimated USD conversions! C
 anadian Locals: If you are based in Canada and experiencing financial barr
 iers\, enter promo code CANADALOCAL at checkout to unlock our $20 CAD supp
 ort tier. --- Live on Zoom. Recording available to ticketholders for 14 da
 ys after class! Get the Total Desire Pass to save on all 5 classes in the 
 Psychology &amp\; Instinct Winter Electives Series! --- Animal Role Play c
 an be a vehicle for stress relief\, structure\, silliness\, and more - but
  it can also be a powerful means of exploring and validating the diverse\,
  often-fluid fabrics of gender and sexuality. In this class\, we&#x27\;ll 
 take a deep dive into how animal role play can relate to gender and sexual
 ity: Finding your animal headspace/s and how they relate to this lens Solo
  play self-connection techniques Centering validation (whether that looks 
 loving or humiliating) in our scenes and dynamics Negotiation tips specifi
 c to navigating gender Exploration and validation for Handlers\, and more.
  This is a discussion-encouraged class to welcome a tapestry of unique exp
 eriences into our content\, but can also be enjoyed by just listening in. 
 There will also be a worksheet to help you apply the ideas to your own hea
 dspace. Let&#x27\;s discover all the ways to help all animal role players 
 feel empowered and seen. --- Get the Total Desire Pass to save on all 5 cl
 asses in the Psychology &amp\; Instinct Series! This also includes a FREE 
 month of the new Wolfe Academy of Desire Patreon + 15% off a one-on-one co
 aching session. If you missed one of the live class date\, you&#x27\;ll st
 ill get a whole month&#x27\;s access to the class via your free Patreon mo
 nth! --- About the Instructor Wiley Wolfe (they/them) is a Primal Handler\
 , kink educator\, coach\, and community organizer based in Toronto\, Canad
 a\, and the founder of the online kink education platform the Wolfe Academ
 y of Desire. They bring 9+ years of experience as a Pro Dominant and kink 
 professional\, over a decade of professional experience screenwriting and 
 developing content for Hollywood film and television\, and a BA in Film wi
 th a minor in Literature. Their kink workshops have been sought after acro
 ss the U.S. and Canada\, including at Dark Odyssey\, Kinkfest\, and Westco
 ast Bound\, with their online classes reaching kinksters worldwide. They h
 ave worked with hundreds of clients\, organized 70+ community events\, led
  support groups\, created erotic immersive theatre productions\, and more.
  They are currently pursuing a master’s-equivalent certification in sex 
 coaching\, and their personal relationships all center power exchange\, qu
 eerness\, polyamory\, and risk-informed consent. Primal and pet play are t
 wo of their deepest passions\, and they actively use both their Handler an
 d primal headspaces as a way to explore\, affirm\, and fuck with their own
  gender alongside those of their playmates&#x27\;. Their approach is a con
 coction of creativity\, real-life animal research\, and our internalized s
 ymbolic templates. They delight in guiding both new and experienced player
 s on their journeys\, with a particular focus on self-exploration\, deepen
 ing intention\, and personal growth. Access: This class is offered live an
 d online through Zoom. You may need to download the free\, basic version o
 f the Zoom app to join. The class will be recorded with the recording avai
 lable to ticketholders for 14 days. After that time\, the recording will b
 e available on Patreon for all tiers that have access to the archive. Reco
 rdings will not include any open group shares at the end of class. The han
 dout accompanying this class will be downloadable for ticketholders to kee
 p. Zoom now provides closed captioning which will be available for this ev
 ent. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/exploring-gender-and-sexuality-through-ani
 mal-role-play
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
